WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.832
An S M executes the threads in a block in

00:00:03.832 --> 00:00:06.497
groups called warps. In the eight rows by

00:00:06.497 --> 00:00:08.829
thirty-two columns case, the block has one

00:00:08.829 --> 00:00:11.162
warp. Each lane identifies one thread in

00:00:11.162 --> 00:00:11.828
that warp.

00:00:13.328 --> 00:00:16.241
A word offset counts four byte values from

00:00:16.241 --> 00:00:19.154
the start of the array. The first eight

00:00:19.154 --> 00:00:20.974
lanes read consecutive columns. Their

00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:23.523
eight values fit in one thirty-two byte

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:23.887
sector.

00:00:25.387 --> 00:00:28.402
The transpose swaps row and column. In the

00:00:28.402 --> 00:00:30.664
output, these lanes write eight words

00:00:30.664 --> 00:00:33.302
apart. The same eight lanes now touch

00:00:33.302 --> 00:00:34.433
eight distinct sectors.

00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:39.014
Across all lanes, the addresses cover four

00:00:39.014 --> 00:00:41.655
read sectors and thirty-two write sectors.

00:00:41.655 --> 00:00:43.856
The calculation groups addresses. Measured

00:00:43.856 --> 00:00:47.377
GPU traffic also depends on caches and the

00:00:47.377 --> 00:00:49.138
instructions the hardware runs.
